    {
      "path": "support/vmm/GATES.md",
      "absolute_path": "/workspace/scratch/ae1a8cf05419/trillionnium-os-desktop/support/vmm/GATES.md",
      "source_sha256": "3ffe2e02c6aa4da993198b331a1ae86fffaba76a40cccbd4fd54117aaa554230",
      "line_start": 6,
      "line_end": 16,
      "lines": [
        {
          "line": 6,
          "text": "| --- | --- | --- |"
        },
        {
          "line": 7,
          "text": "| Intel VMX | ostd/src/arch/x86/vm/mod.rs, context.rs, ept.rs, vmx/ and ostd/src/vm/{gpm_space,guest_mode}.rs provide Intel VMX, EPT, guest context/exit primitives | No Linux boot VMM, PCI GPU passthrough, vCPU scheduling, virt IRQ, device model, recovery qualification |"
        },
        {
          "line": 8,
          "text": "| AMD SVM | No SVM-specific file in pinned x86 vm tree; implementation uses VMX/VMCS | Do not use VMX example as proof of AMD SVM/NPT/VMCB/VMRUN, even though visible virtual CPU is AMD |"
        },
        {
          "line": 9,
          "text": "| ARM EL2 | No ARM VM implementation found in pinned VM path | No ARM EL2, stage-2/SMMU/GIC guest virtualization pass |"
        },
        {
          "line": 10,
          "text": "| IOMMU | ostd/src/arch/x86/iommu/{dma_remapping,interrupt_remapping,invalidate,fault,registers} source surfaces exist | Not a complete GPU assignment API, validated IOMMU group/isolation, reset or AMD-Vi evidence |"
        },
        {
          "line": 11,
          "text": ""
        },
        {
          "line": 12,
          "text": "Execution-tool container: Linux 6.18.44, x86_64, no /dev/kvm, no forwarded vmx/svm flags; NO hypervisor run. Upstream osdk/tests/examples_in_book/write_a_hypervisor_in_100_lines_templates/lib.rs demonstrates a small VMX real-mode guest that prints serial and halts; not a Linux guest VM or a GPU VMM."
        },
        {
          "line": 13,
          "text": ""
        },
        {
          "line": 14,
          "text": "## Mandatory engineering gates for selected route C"
        },
        {
          "line": 15,
          "text": ""
        },
        {
          "line": 16,
          "text": "1. Discover actual architecture at runtime; reject VMX absent on Intel / SVM absent on AMD. If AMD target is chosen, implement/test SVM instead of attempting VMX commands. No aggressive emulation fallback."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "path": "support/hardware/DECISION.md",
      "absolute_path": "/workspace/scratch/ae1a8cf05419/trillionnium-os-desktop/support/hardware/DECISION.md",
      "source_sha256": "d59600c17d4145ebdeb349ffa94e7b1c9cfa83a0bec567ff352d28c0f02eed4a",
      "line_start": 5,
      "line_end": 9,
      "lines": [
        {
          "line": 5,
          "text": "## Actual authorized observation vs candidate"
        },
        {
          "line": 6,
          "text": ""
        },
        {
          "line": 7,
          "text": "The read-only probe ran in the execution-tool Linux container, NOT on a user-provided bare-metal GPU host. Visible environment: Linux 6.18.44, x86_64, virtual CPU model AMD EPYC 9V74 80-Core Processor (3 visible /proc/cpuinfo processor entries, not a claim about physical cores). PCI enumeration exposed host bridge 8086:0d57 and six VirtIO functions: 1af4:1042, 1af4:1041, 1af4:1044, 1af4:105b, 1af4:1053, 1af4:1045. No visible PCI display or compute-accelerator class, NVIDIA or AMD GPU, /dev/dri/renderD128, /dev/kfd, /dev/nvidiactl, /dev/nvidia0, /dev/vfio/vfio or /dev/kvm. No VMX/SVM flags, visible IOMMU group or DMAR/IVRS table. Absence in a restricted container DOES NOT prove physical host absence."
        },
        {
          "line": 8,
          "text": ""
        },
        {
          "line": 9,
          "text": "The real GPU's PCI vendor/device/subsystem IDs and BDF, GPU/NPU ID, loaded GSP/other firmware, driver version, IOMMU/interrupt remapping, VRAM/UMA topology, DMA reachability, command submission, queue count, synchronization/fences, reset availability and safety, and CUDA runtime version remain UNKNOWN/UNOBSERVED. They MUST NOT be fabricated from marketing specifications or another machine. See ../../tests/hardware/evidence/2026-10-16-container-probe.json."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "path": "docs/HARDWARE_AND_DRIVERS.md",
      "absolute_path": "/workspace/scratch/ae1a8cf05419/trillionnium-os-desktop/docs/HARDWARE_AND_DRIVERS.md",
      "source_sha256": "d31ad12248e97ca7cefdb98bc386fe5e0e3158dfbd131a281e6556cdd5bbcad3",
      "line_start": 35,
      "line_end": 39,
      "lines": [
        {
          "line": 35,
          "text": "## 6. VMM不是免费备选"
        },
        {
          "line": 36,
          "text": ""
        },
        {
          "line": 37,
          "text": "OSTD虚拟化基础与完整VMM/虚拟中断/设备模型/KVM兼容接口分开；Intel VMX、AMD SVM、ARM EL2分别核对源码和硬件前提。当前固定上游不等于本项目已支持任意后端。[OSTD RFC](SOURCES.md#ostd-vmm)"
        },
        {
          "line": 38,
          "text": ""
        },
        {
          "line": 39,
          "text": "只把VM列为允许路径，未完成具体后端/设备验证前不承诺“全Linux/Android可用”。调试用Linux/KVM宿主与最终由新内核托管VM是不同实验。"
        }
      ]
    }
